Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-650d43b4-070d-4425-a165-f85f53204309', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are the Itinerary Finalizer for PariKrama, an Indian travel planning system.\n\nCreate a detailed day-by-day travel itinerary using all the research and booking data provided.\n\nFor EACH day, include:\n- title: "Day 1: Arrival & Local Exploration" (creative, descriptive)\n- activities: list of {time, activity, location, cost_inr, duration_mins, tips}\n- meals: list of {time, type (breakfast/lunch/dinner), suggestion, estimated_cost_inr}\n- accommodation: {hotel, check_in (Day 1 only), check_out (last day only)}\n- estimated_cost_inr: total estimated spend for the day\n- tips: list of practical tips for the day\n\nStyle guidelines:\n- Friendly, conversational tone — like advice from a seasoned Indian traveler\n- Include local food recommendations (specific dishes, dhaba vs restaurant)\n- Mention photography spots with best lighting time\n- Budget travel tips (shared cabs, local buses, packed lunch)\n- Consider weather (no outdoor activities during peak heat or rain)\n- Buffer time for rest and spontaneous exploration\n- Hindi phrases helpful for locals (optional, 1-2 per day)\n\nReturn a JSON array of day plan objects, one per day.\nNo markdown, no explanation — only the JSON array starting with [.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "Create a 5-day itinerary for this trip:\n\nTrip: Delhi → Manali, 5 days\nBudget: ₹15,000 for 1 traveler(s)\nStyle: budget\n\nWeather: Day 1: 34.6-35.5C, Day 2: 28.9-28.9C, Day 3: 30.5-30.5C, Day 4: 30.4-30.4C, Day 5: 30.2-30.2C\nAdvisory: Pleasant temperatures — light cotton clothing is fine; carry rain gear and waterproof covers for bags; temperatures drop sharply after sunset even in summer — always carry a jacket.\n\nTop Places:\n  - Rohtang Pass (scenic, ₹550 entry, best: morning)\n  - Solang Valley (adventure, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Hadimba Devi Temple (temple, ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Mall Road (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: evening)\n  - Beas River Rafting (adventure, ₹600 entry, best: morning)\n  - Old Manali (culture, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Vashisht Hot Springs (wellness, ₹50 entry, best: morning)\n\nResearch Brief:\n**Manali Research Brief: 5-Day Budget Trip**\n\n**Weather Summary:**\nManali's weather is pleasant during your 5-day trip, with temperatures ranging from 28.9°C to 35.5°C. However, be prepared for sudden rain showers and temperature drops after sunset. Pack light cotton clothing, rain gear, and waterproof covers for your bags. Don't forget to carry a jacket for cooler evenings.\n\n**Best Time for Activities:**\nPlan your outdoor activities like hiking, rafting, or visiting Rohtang Pass during the morning or early afternoon when the sun is out. As the temperature drops in the evening, explore Mall Road, Old Manali, or visit the Hadimba Devi Temple.\n\n**Top Attractions:**\nRanked by must-visit priority, here are the top attractions in Manali:\n\n1. **Rohtang Pass** (scenic, 550 INR entry): A must-visi\n\nRecommended Hotel: Backpacker's Inn Manali (₹650/night, rating: 3.8)\nRecommended Transport: bus (₹650, 14 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹1,300, Hotel ₹3,250, Food ₹3,750, Activities ₹1,000"}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'max_tokens': 2048, 'temperature': 0.7}}
