 ₹0 entry, best: morning)\n  - Anjuna Flea Market (shopping, ₹0 entry, best: afternoon)\n  - Fort Aguada (heritage, ₹35 entry, best: evening)\n\nResearch Brief:\n**Goa Research Brief: 5-Day Budget Trip**\n\n**Weather Summary and Packing**\nThe weather forecast for your 5-day trip to Goa indicates pleasant temperatures ranging from 23.3°C to 23.9°C. Pack light cotton clothing, and don't forget to carry rain gear and waterproof covers for your bags. Although it's not peak monsoon season, it's always a good idea to be prepared for unexpected showers.\n\n**Best Time for Activities**\nThe best time to visit Goa is typically between November and May, but since you're traveling during a relatively cooler period, you can enjoy outdoor activities like trekking, kayaking, or simply exploring the beaches. Try to visit popular spots like Fort Aguada and Basilica of Bom Jesus during cooler hours (early morning or late afternoon) to avoid the heat.\n\n**Top Attractions \n\nRecommended Hotel: Backpacker's Inn Goa (₹650/night, rating: 3.8)\nRecommended Transport: train (₹450, 8.0 hrs)\n\nBudget Breakdown: Transport ₹1,800, Hotel ₹2,600, Food ₹4,500, Activities ₹1,000"}], 'model': 'llama-3.3-70b-versatile', 'max_tokens': 8192, 'temperature': 0.7}}
